+//! The API as a contract: one document, published by the service, that says what every route takes
+//! and answers.
+//!
+//! Step `relay/2.3-contract-first` implements it. "Hand-written" means written here, once, by a
+//! function that returns the same value every time it is called — not typed twice, and not pasted
+//! from a wiki. The service publishes it at `GET /openapi.json`, so a client reads what this
+//! service promises instead of reading its source.
+//!
+//! What makes it a contract rather than decoration is where the spec looks: the routes it declares
+//! have to be the routes the router serves, the fields it calls `required` have to be the fields
+//! the handlers demand, every schema has to declare its `type`, and every `$ref` has to land on a
+//! schema the document declares.
+//!
+//! One decision is yours before you write a line of it: where the *names* live. A route, a schema
+//! and the field lists they share can be spelled once and referred to, or spelled three times and
+//! kept in step by hand — and the step's TRAP is what happens to the second one.
+
